Section 3 - Scope
(5)
This Policy applies to:
all staff or contractors delivering training and assessment in the Cert IV ACHM;
other La Trobe staff associated with the delivery of the Cert IV ACHM and of relevant student services;
all students enrolled in the Cert IV ACHM.

Section 5 - Policy Statement
(6)
The La Trobe RTO ensures that students enrolled in the Cert IV ACHM have a quality student experience and are supported to achieve the competencies required for successful completion of the course. This is achieved by:
the provision of comprehensive course material that is clear, accurate and current for the applicable course occurrence;
rigorous and culturally sensitive selection processes to ensure students are qualified and equipped to successfully complete the course;
thorough, consistent and transparent processes for the granting of credit and Recognition of Prior Learning (RPL);
ensuring culturally safe and culturally responsive learning environments, recognising and valuing Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander cultures, and supporting practices that promote safety, respect and inclusion for all learners, including the provision of Reasonable Adjustments;
access to all student support resources of La Trobe University;
access to fair and equitable processes to seek a review of any decision affecting them.

Minimum Entry Requirements
(15)
All applicants must be:
an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander;
over 18 years of age prior to course commencement;
able to read, write and speak English at a level that will enable them to participate in and compete the requirements of the course, as evidenced by the results of a Learning, Literacy and Numeracy (LLN) test based on the AQF foundation skill levels identified for the Cert IV ACHM.
(16)
The VET Senior Educator, together with the VET Program Manager, conduct the initial screening of applicants for the course to determine initial eligibility. For all applicants this involves:
testing of learning, literacy and numeracy proficiency via their performance in an LLN test;
an interview;
consideration of whether they have successfully completed the FPSR three-day introductory Aboriginal Cultural Heritage Management workshop.

Part C - Credit and Recognition of Prior Learning
(21)
The La Trobe RTO:
recognises all qualifications recognised by the Australian Qualifications Framework, and Records of Results and Statements of Attainment issued by any other Registered Training Organisations;
provides written advice about its processes for Recognition of Prior Learning (RPL) and credit for previous relevant VET study when an offer is made to students;
maintains records of credit and RPL claims and outcomes in relevant student files.

Fee Conditions
(28)
The La Trobe RTO establishes:
the method of advice of fees payable;
the date for payment of fees;
the circumstances in which a fee may be waived, deferred or refunded;
administrative and miscellaneous fines and charges;
circumstances under which fees may be paid under a payment plan.
